<title>SINGAPORE: World rice prices - January 16.</title>
<headline>World rice prices - January 16.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rice prices quoted by trading and official sources in the key producing nations of Thailand, Vietnam, India and the United States in U.S. dollars a tonne:</p>
<p>							     Jan 16    Jan 9</p>
<p>Thailand-100 pct white B benchmark FOB Bangkok 380-400   370-400</p>
<p>Thailand-100 pct fragrant rice FOB Bangkok     620-640   620-625</p>
<p>India-25 pct broken(non-Basmati loong grain)FOB 230	 230</p>
<p>India-15-10 pct broken FOB (west coast port)   245-280   250-285</p>
<p>Vietnam-5.0 percent broken FOB Saigon port     268-270   275-280</p>
<p>Vietnam-10 percent broken FOB Saigon port	 258	265-268</p>
<p>U.S.-California medium grain ($ per cwt) 21.00-22.00 19.50-20.50  </p>
<p>U.S.-Long grain Arkansas ($ per cwt)     21.00-22.00 19.50-20.50</p>
